<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal one-day rail strike called for Friday.</title>
<headline>Portugal one-day rail strike called for Friday.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Train services were set to be disrupted on Friday due to a one-day strike called by several unions to protest against a restructuring of railway company Caminhos de Ferro Portugueses (CP), a CP official source said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are expecting Lisbon-Oporto and inter-city services to be severely disrupted and some suburban services to be affected,&quot; the source told Reuters.</p>
<p>Unions have called the stoppage to press for improved career structures and to protest against plans to restructure CP.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
